{%- comment -%}
  BreadcrumbList JSON-LD (Citadel brief §06: "BreadcrumbList on all";
  brief v4 §21).

  Two modes:
  1. Default (no crumbs param): two-level Home -> {page title}, using
     the current page. Backward compatible with the existing callers
     (about, destinations-index, clinicians, book, contact pages).
  2. Custom (crumbs param): N-level breadcrumb. Pass a string of
     "Label::path" pairs separated by "|", e.g.
        crumbs: 'Home::/|Travel vaccinations::/pages/travel-vaccinations|Typhoid::/pages/typhoid'
     Paths may be root-relative (a leading "/" is fine) or absolute.
     Used by the vaccine-hub and traveller-type templates so the schema
     matches their visible three-level breadcrumb nav.

  Renders nothing outside a page context to stay safe if accidentally
  included on the wrong template.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if request.page_type == 'page' and page.handle != blank -%}
  {%- if crumbs != blank -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Pre-validate before opening the script tag: only a pair with both
      a non-blank name and a non-blank path becomes a ListItem (Google
      Breadcrumbs requirement -- every itemListElement needs a non-empty
      name). Counted first so a crumbs string that resolves to zero
      valid pairs emits no BreadcrumbList at all, rather than an empty
      or malformed one.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign crumb_pairs = crumbs | split: '|' -%}
    {%- assign valid_crumb_count = 0 -%}
    {%- for pair in crumb_pairs -%}
      {%- assign bits = pair | split: '::' -%}
      {%- assign precheck_name = bits[0] | strip -%}
      {%- assign precheck_path = bits[1] | strip -%}
      {%- if precheck_name != blank and precheck_path != blank -%}
        {%- assign valid_crumb_count = valid_crumb_count | plus: 1 -%}
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
    {%- if valid_crumb_count > 0 -%}
    <script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    {%- assign pos = 0 -%}
    {%- for pair in crumb_pairs -%}
      {%- assign bits = pair | split: '::' -%}
      {%- assign crumb_name = bits[0] | strip -%}
      {%- assign crumb_path = bits[1] | strip -%}
      {%- if crumb_name != blank and crumb_path != blank -%}
        {%- assign pos = pos | plus: 1 -%}
        {%- unless pos == 1 %},{% endunless -%}
        {%- if crumb_path contains '://' -%}
          {%- assign crumb_url = crumb_path -%}
        {%- else -%}
          {%- assign crumb_url = shop.url | append: crumb_path -%}
        {%- endif -%}
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": {{ pos }}, "name": {{ crumb_name | json }}, "item": {{ crumb_url | json }} }
      {%- endif -%}
    {%- endfor -%}
  ]
}
    </script>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- elsif page.title != blank -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Google Breadcrumbs requires a non-empty name on every
      itemListElement. "Home" is a hardcoded literal (always valid);
      page.title is the only variable value here, so the whole
      BreadcrumbList is withheld rather than emitting a ListItem with
      a blank name if a page ever has no title set.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <script type="application/ld+json">
{
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
  "itemListElement": [
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "{{ shop.url }}" },
    { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": {{ page.title | json }}, "item": "{{ shop.url }}{{ page.url }}" }
  ]
}
    </script>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}
